e top) and throttle the review-bot, the exact component-coupling the mcp block was designed to avoid (see the MCP_BACKOFF_FILE comment at autodeploy.sh:65-70).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8a63d0d8d42de57c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach ('The deploy gate closes as the store gate did (autodeploy.sh step 5b)') and Scope (infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh)","norm_id":"nc08202e4969fca74","priority":0.7,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A blue-green container reports handshake.ok=false; the new gate fires record_backoff_failure, writing the bot backoff file and suppressing an unrelated review-bot deploy on subsequent ticks"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the new gate, on handshake.ok present-and-false call `record_mcp_backoff_failure` before `exit 1`, matching every other failure branch in the mcp block; note the 5b store gate should be corrected the same way.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify gate behavior under auth: suppress the handshake field (or set ok absent) when RequireAuthMiddleware/ProxyAuthMiddleware is active so an auth-enabled boot promotes, rather than reporting ok=false and blocking every deploy.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T12"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1722,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the server holds no credential to present to itself, so an auth-enabled boot would always report failure'","Plan: 'refuse the upstream flip when handshake.ok is present and false'","Absence: no statement of whether an auth-enabled server sets handshake.ok=false (blocking all deploys) or omits the field (promotes)"],"finding":"The plan states an auth-enabled boot 'would always report failure' because the server holds no credential to present to itself, yet the deploy gate refuses promotion whenever handshake.ok is present and false. On any auth-enabled server this makes the gate block EVERY promotion, turning the safety check into a total deploy freeze. The plan does not specify how the gate distinguishes 'handshake failed because misconfigured' from 'handshake failed because auth is on' — i.e. whether the handshake field is suppressed (absent, so promotes) when RequireAuthMiddleware/ProxyAuthMiddleware is active.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f316fdd58ced30f40","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — 'Conclusive.' Boundary paragraph + Approach 'The deploy gate closes as the store gate did'","norm_id":"n3a2ccc3a87fc7cd7","priority":0.7778,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"When install_startup_handshake detects the ProxyAuthMiddleware/RequireAuthMiddleware wrapper is present, skip the drive and omit the handshake field (treated as mixed-version-absent -> promotes), and add an acceptance criterion asserting an auth-enabled boot still promotes.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"veri